        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d46d1ece-33e2-566a-91db-b9b45aa0610f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: The Strongest Man in the World, Candleshoe, Now You See Him, Now You Don't, The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes\n- People: Kurt Russell, Jodie Foster, David Niven, Helen Hayes, Leo McKern, John Alderson, Michael Innes\n- Organizations: Walt Disney Productions\n- Places: Medfield College\n- Topics: film sequels, acting careers\n\nFacts:\n- The 1969 film \"The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes\" was followed by the sequel \"Now You See Him, Now You Don't.\"\n- \"The Strongest Man in the World\" followed \"Now You See Him, Now You Don't\" in 1975.\n- \"The Strongest Man in the World\" is a 1975 Disney film starring Kurt Russell as a student at the fictional Medfield College.\n- John Alderson was an English actor born on 10 April 1916 and died on 4 August 2006.\n- John Alderson played the lead in the 1957–58 syndicated western television series \"Boots and Saddles,\" which ran for thirty-eight episodes in a single season.\n- John Alderson had a film and television acting career from 1951 to 1990 and appeared in \"Candleshoe\" in 1977.\n- \"Candleshoe\" is a 1977 American family adventure film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- \"Candleshoe\" was based on Michael Innes's novel \"Christmas at Candleshoe\" and starred Jodie Foster, David Niven, Helen Hayes in her last big-screen appearance, and Leo McKern.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
